  "learningOutcomes": "By the end of the sub-strand, the learner should be able to:\na) describe the reflection of waves and relate it to echoes in the environment,\nb) investigate refraction of waves in different media and apply it to lenses and everyday observations,\nc) explain diffraction of waves around obstacles and through gaps,\nd) investigate interference of waves and the formation of interference patterns,\ne) describe the formation of stationary waves and their relationship to resonance and musical pitch,\nf) explain the Doppler effect and its applications,\ng) relate wave properties to technologies in communication and medicine,\nh) appreciate the need to reduce noise pollution in the environment.\n\nKey concepts: waves transfer energy without transferring matter; reflection, refraction, diffraction and interference are wave behaviours that can be predicted with models; frequency, wavelength, speed and amplitude link to what we hear and see; the Doppler shift depends on relative motion.",
