  "supportingPhenomena": "• Refraction in water and lenses: a straw in a glass of water appears bent, and lenses focus light to form images in glasses, cameras and microscopes, as when a fisherman at Lake Victoria misjudges the depth of a fish.\n• Diffraction of sound and light: sound is heard around corners of a classroom block and light bends slightly around edges.\n• Interference patterns: ripples on water or overlapping sound waves create patterns of reinforcement and cancellation, as in noise-cancelling headphones.\n• Stationary waves and resonance: vibrating strings or air columns produce standing waves with nodes and antinodes, as in the nyatiti, guitar and flute.\n• Doppler effect: the pitch of an ambulance siren on Thika Road changes as it passes by.\n• Wave applications in communication and medicine: radio waves carry FM radio and mobile phone signals, and ultrasound produces images of internal organs.\n• Noise pollution: traffic in Nairobi, matatu hooters and industrial sounds affect human health.",
